:"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:99b00227799d0433d0a70859296c836b0d183356480bba3309cc75837a2a4f51","file":"preprints/The-maximal-triangular-Hilbert-transform-at-the-symmetric-point-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":16,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1602aa6ad3e19b62770e9bf06e82278957bdd7dcb98cd19c1409aee64f7f073d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-maximal-triangular-Hilbert-transform-at-the-symmetric-point-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:99b00227799d0433d0a70859296c836b0d183356480bba3309cc75837a2a4f51","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-maximal-triangular-Hilbert-transform-at-the-symmetric-point-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L16"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is an absolute constant $C$ such that, for every pair of complex\nfunctions $F,G\\in L^3(\\R^2)$,\n\\[\n \\|B_*(F,G)\\|_{L^{3/2}(\\R^2)}\n \\le C\\|F\\|_{L^3(\\R^2)}\\|G\\|_{L^3(\\R^2)}.\n\\]\nThe supremum is over both finite hard truncation endpoints."}
